          "q": "Can an NRI get a Lower Deduction Certificate, and do I need to visit India?",
          "a": "<p><strong>Yes. An NRI selling property can apply under Section 395(1) of the Income Tax Act, 2025, using Form 128, the successor to Form 13. You do not need to visit India: the application, officer queries and certificate download happen online through the TRACES taxpayer login, and a professional can act for you.</strong> Any person, resident or non-resident, can apply under <a href=\"https://www.incometaxindia.gov.in/w/section-395-6\">Section 395</a>. Filing is optional and is done only on TRACES: log in, go to Dashboard, then e-file and view, then File Forms, then Form 128. A PAN is mandatory, and on submission you receive an Acknowledgment Receipt Number. The application must include a computation of estimated income and tax for the year. Registration of the sale deed follows the local registrar's rules, so a registered power of attorney may be needed if you cannot attend. Source: <a href=\"https://www.incometaxindia.gov.in/documents/d/guest/form-128-faqs\">Form 128 FAQs, Income Tax Department</a>. <em>Read more:</em> <a href=\"https://cashstreamadvisors.com/international-taxation/lower-deduction-certificate/\">Lower Deduction Certificate for NRI property sale</a></p>"
