          "a": "<p><strong>Yes. An NRI must report the sale in an Indian income tax return, usually due by 31 July after the financial year, even if a certificate was used. Late or missed filing can lead to scrutiny proceedings for the year of sale and penalties, and it is also the only route to a refund.</strong> Use a professional for the return, because the capital gains computation must match the figures used in the certificate and the buyer's TDS return.</p>"
